import json
from pathlib import Path
W=Path(__file__).resolve().parent;b=json.loads((W/'inventory-before.json').read_text('utf8'))
f={
'fiscal-policy-and-aggregate-demand':('F','Hard already includes direct versus tax-induced spending, MPC inference and opposing policy changes. Several Legendary items merely repeat first-round calculations or policy recognition. Strengthen selected package/allocation constraints without moving tiers.'),
'fiscal-multipliers-and-crowding-out':('C,D,F','Basic multipliers are available at Medium/Hard. However, graph-linked Hard questions mostly identify curve order; add normal multiplier-plus-graph application at Hard. A recurring ambiguity treats a raw investment decline as an already-multiplied AD offset. Specify total-AD versus autonomous offsets. Upper items frequently repeat simple arithmetic. Partial crowding out alone does not guarantee a final position between AD2 and AD3.'),
'stabilization-policy':('D,F','Strong Hard policy-lag, demand/supply dilemma and combined-impulse applications exist. Several numeric items equate a horizontal AD shift with a realized output-gap change without a fixed-price assumption. Preserve supplied monetary shocks, avoid reauthoring money mechanics, and strengthen fiscal timing/offset synthesis.'),
'aggregate-demand':('D,F','Hard covers determinants, joint changes and movement versus shift. The hand-drawn numeric AD assets warrant approximate readings, not falsely exact values. Upper graph records repeat basic recognition; add reverse determination with the existing images.'),
'short-run-aggregate-supply':('D,F','Hard sticky-wage and opposed-cost scenarios are substantial. AS-01 is hand-drawn: its intercept is around 70, not exactly 75, and the apparent vertical separation is about 40–45, not exactly 40. Use defensible approximations and remove economic conclusions from metadata. Strengthen selected upper expectations/supply comparisons.'),
'long-run-aggregate-supply-and-potential-output':('D,F','Coverage exists despite the smaller module. Hard labor-force plus energy-cost items assert SRAS left without stating which opposing effect dominates. Clarify that assumption. The capital-productivity percentage scenario needs a defined capacity relation before a numerical conclusion; use an explicit physical-capacity accounting model.'),
'ad-as-equilibrium-and-output-gaps':('G','Graph equilibrium/gap identification and Hard permanent-capacity-versus-old-potential diagnosis are adequate. Keep the distinctions and source-objective aliases; graph metadata needs assessment-safe evidence without diagnostic conclusions.'),
'demand-and-supply-shocks':('D,F','Hard already gives joint output/price outcomes, simultaneous shifts and supply-shock policy tradeoffs. ECON-SP-HARD-212 starts at AS2 but claims another displayed increase to AS2; correct the start/end comparison. Upper graph records often repeat simpler interpretations; selectively require reverse shifts and policy constraints.'),
'long-run-macroeconomic-self-adjustment':('D,F','Hard has full positive/negative demand adjustment chains. Some items call demand shocks temporary but then retain their post-shock AD level forever. State persistence of the demand shift. Upper policy versus self-correction comparisons need distinguish shared output restoration from opposite price effects; deepen selected graph/path inference.')}
out=[]
for c,m in b['views'].items():
 for objective,count in b['byConcept'][c]['objectives'].items():
  codes,reason=f.get(c,('G','Selected by the live preset but protected for the later dedicated Phillips audit. Reviewed only for AD-AS integration consistency; no new cross-system defect identified. This is not a claim that the Phillips bank has received a fresh full content-quality audit.'))
  rows=[q for q in b['records'].values() if q['primaryConceptId']==c and q['objective']==objective]
  out.append({'concept':c,'objective':objective,'label':m['objectiveLabels'].get(objective,objective),'count':count,'classifications':codes.split(','),'finding':reason,'coverageGap':False,'reviewDepth':'full content' if c in f else 'integration only / deferred','evidenceIds':[q['id'] for q in rows if q.get('canonicalDifficulty') in ['hard','elite','legendary']][:8]})
(W/'objective-findings-before.json').write_text(json.dumps(out,indent=2,ensure_ascii=False)+'\n','utf8')
(W/'OBJECTIVE_FINDINGS_BEFORE.md').write_text('# Findings before authoring\n\n'+ '\n\n'.join(f"## {x['concept']} / {x['objective']}\n\n{x['count']} records; {','.join(x['classifications'])}; {x['reviewDepth']}. {x['finding']}" for x in out)+'\n\nNo materially absent objective or missing graph family was identified. Accuracy/precision, localized Hard graph integration and repeated upper-tier grammars justify targeted revisions. All 20 distinct used image files (27 registrations) were visually inspected; Phillips contracts remain deferred. No production content has been authored at this point.\n','utf8')
print(len(out),'concept/objective findings')
